        "geoBonBiome": [
          "Terrestrial"
        ],
        "geology": "The bedrock is mainly composed of Hercynian Ca-poor granite (315 ± 7 Myr), which has been subjected to hydrothermal alterations of various levels with main hydrothermal alterations occurring 183,9 My ago. In addition to granite, which is heavily hydrothermally altered on the south-facing slope and less altered on the north-facing slope, small microgranite and gneiss bodies outcrop along the southern and northern slopes, respectively.",
        "hydrology": "The mean annual discharge at the outlet for the 1986-2015 period is of about 750 mm (24.5 ls-1km-2) with variations ranging from 494 to 1132 mm/yr. The outlet discharge varied between 1 l/s up to 400 l/s during high flow discharge corresponding particularly to rain events associated with snow melting periods.",
        "soils": "brown acidic to ochreous podzolic soils.\r\nSoils of the watershed are brown acidic to ochreous podzolic and are generally roughly 1 meter thick. The soils are very coarsely grained, sandy and rich in gravel. Soil pH levels range from 3.5 at the surface to 4.5 at 1 m deep. ",
        "vegetation": "The forest covers 90% of the area with approximately 80% of the area including spruce trees (mainly Piceas Abies L.) and of the area 20% supporting beech trees (Fagus Sylvatica). The catchment is used as a commercially managed forest and plantations range in age from 50 to 145 years. Forest decline related to acid precipitation was observed in the Strengbach Catchment in the 1980s."
      },
